    "title": "Forget Lake Tahoe, California's Lake Getaway Just Outside Stockton Has Serene Swims And Nature Walks - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Audrey Simons ,\n1 days ago Lake Tahoe is pretty much the poster child for California's alpine beauty. The place is famed for its clear blue waters, surrounded by stately pine trees and snow-capped mountain vistas. But it's also notorious for big crowds, welcoming millions of visitors each year. If you don't mind a change of scenery, you can find a far quieter spot nearby at Lodi Lake. This water haven sits only about 2.5 hours southwest of its famous Tahoe counterpart, in the flatlands of California's Central Valley. Read full article\n7",
